## Original Content
Chinese President Xi Jinping held talks with visiting King of the Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan Abdullah II ibn Al Hussein at the Great Hall of the People in Beijing on Monday afternoon.

## Summary
Chinese President Xi Jinping met with King Abdullah II ibn Al Hussein of Jordan at the Great Hall of the People in Beijing. The talks focused on deepening the alignment of development strategies between China and Jordan.

## Key Points
- Xi Jinping held talks with King Abdullah II ibn Al Hussein during a visit to Beijing.
- The discussion emphasized the importance of aligning development strategies between China and Jordan.
- The meeting took place at the Great Hall of the People, highlighting diplomatic engagement.


